## The Design Rule: Default to Refraction

TuffEx's design rules say that a container with a surface layer defaults to `refraction`, so that the whole system shares one visual signature instead of each component choosing its own.

The component defaults follow the rule: `TxBaseSurface`'s `mode`, `TxCard`'s `background`, `TxFlipOverlay`'s `surface`, and the `panelBackground` of the pop-up panels in the table above (which all render through `TxBaseAnchor`) are all `refraction`. Dialogs and drawers such as `TxModal` and `TxDrawer` do not go through `TxBaseSurface` and have no mode to choose.

## Explicit Confirmation Gatekeeper for Mode Switching

If a specialized scenario demands switching the material (`mode`, `background`, `surface` or `panelBackground`) from `refraction` to another one (such as `pure`, `mask`, `blur` or `glass`):
- **Explicit manual user confirmation is mandatory**!
- Neither AI coding agents nor engineers may arbitrarily override the default material.
- This gatekeeper preserves design system integrity across distributed teams and automated workflows.
